The finished website should feel like a premium modern Islamic educational institution's digital platform.

It must be:

- Beautiful.
- Trustworthy.
- Professional.
- Elegant.
- Fast.
- Mobile-friendly.
- Secure.
- Fully manageable.
- Future-ready.

The overall experience should make parents and visitors feel confident about the institution.

Remember:

This is the official digital identity of Asma Binte Abu Bakr (RA.) Mohila Madrasa.

The design must respect Islamic values, institutional identity, modesty, and professionalism.

Use the real logo and actual photographs provided by the client.

Use the official Bengali name and slogan consistently.

Do not invent facts.

Do not compromise on Bengali typography or Android usability.

Do not confuse the Masala-Masayel Q&A system with the general chatbot or direct live chat.

Do not confuse online admission inquiry with final offline admission.

Do not confuse the main website with the institution's separate mobile app or Web App.

Now begin by analyzing the complete requirements, preparing the project architecture, and creating the design system. Then implement the project systematically.

The final result must be a complete, maintainable, developer-friendly full-stack project rather than a static website demonstration.